    "readme": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1220,
      "w": 440,
      "size": "m",
      "fill": "purple",
      "text": "Read me first\n\nThe app is for people; the CLI is for machines (CI, coding agents, scripts). The TUI is retired once the app matches it. One binary is the CLI, the app and the daemon.\n\nOne window, a tab per stack; opening doze again brings it forward. Installed by drag and drop, then set up in the app on first launch with one admin prompt.\n\nBuilt with Wails v3: Go, and a web view, so doze-aws's and doze-kafka's consoles load inside, in an embedded mode they each gain. Light by rule: one web view, no frontend framework, live data only for what's on screen.\n\nEvery board uses the shop fixture's data. Anything the TUI doesn't have is marked new; the Grounding board says what each new thing is built from, and what work it needs.",
      "page": "daily"
    }
  },
